{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TeDxUniH8ytDfqbxhqyNEX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Epic Fix Batch 1 — from canonical epic review (artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json)\n2\t\n3\tBounded fixes for the current epic-review findings. Each item is in scope for this pass.\n4\t\n5\t- **F-EPIC-001 (blocker)**: `threads.newThread` accepts an empty/blank `filePath` and registers a thread with no durable file. `src/domains/threads/index.ts:73` guards only with `existsSync(filePath)`; `node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync('')` opens a temporary database that vanishes on close, so the operation returns ok and inserts a registry row for `filePath: \"\"`. Fix: reject empty or whitespace-only `filePath` (and any path that cannot produce a durable file) as `caller_error` before touching storage, at the SDK surface so both SDK and CLI get the guard. Add red tests: SDK `newThread({ filePath: \"\" })` → caller_error with nothing created and no registry row; CLI `threads new-thread --file-path ''` → JSON error, exit 1, clean registry. Mirror the check in `resolveThreadRef` for `{ filePath: \"\" }` so read paths fail closed with `caller_error` rather than opening a temp database.\n6\t- **F-EPIC-002**: Read-back surfaces (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listQueuedWork`) skip thread-reference validation present on the write path, so malformed references (e.g. empty path) reach storage open. Fix: route all read surfaces through the same `resolveThreadRef` validation used by writes; empty/invalid refs return `caller_error`/`thread_not_found` consistently at SDK and CLI layers. Add a small test per read surface for the empty-path and unknown-id legs.\n7\t- **NB-2**: CLI parses flags with `strict: false`, silently ignoring unknown or misspelled flags (e.g. `--file-pth`). Fix: enable strict flag parsing in the CLI arg parser and return the existing structured usage error (`caller_error` with the CLI-adapter code pattern) naming the unknown flag; keep exit code 1. Update/extend the CLI process suite leg for an unknown-flag case.\n8\t- **NB-5**: Dead code and stale artifacts. Remove the uncalled `notImplemented()` helper from `shared/errors.ts` (all stubs are gone since Story 5). Clean stale pre-epic compiled output from `dist/` (`dist/commands/`, `dist/thread-events/`, `dist/token-counting/`) — add a `prebuild` clean (e.g. `rm -rf dist` before `tsc`) or equivalent so `dist/` always reflects current `src/`.\n9\t\n10\tOut of scope for this batch (tracked separately): NB-1 (empty-string payload text — pending human ruling on epic-vs-tech-design conflict), NB-4 (test seams are sanctioned by the test plan's architecture-risk rows; no change), work_item constraint vocabulary (Epic 02 owns lifecycle schema).\n11\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36778e1e-3bb5-45c6-8164-3cc17eb2f31a","uuid":"e606bd1e-0415-448f-bc50-cce0a83e11d0","timestamp":"2026-06-10T15:38:03.761Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/fix/001-epic-fix-batch.md","content":"# Epic Fix Batch 1 — from canonical epic review (artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json)\n\nBounded fixes for the current epic-review findings. Each item is in scope for this pass.\n\n- **F-EPIC-001 (blocker)**: `threads.newThread` accepts an empty/blank `filePath` and registers a thread with no durable file. `src/domains/threads/index.ts:73` guards only with `existsSync(filePath)`; `node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync('')` opens a temporary database that vanishes on close, so the operation returns ok and inserts a registry row for `filePath: \"\"`. Fix: reject empty or whitespace-only `filePath` (and any path that cannot produce a durable file) as `caller_error` before touching storage, at the SDK surface so both SDK and CLI get the guard. Add red tests: SDK `newThread({ filePath: \"\" })` → caller_error with nothing created and no registry row; CLI `threads new-thread --file-path ''` → JSON error, exit 1, clean registry. Mirror the check in `resolveThreadRef` for `{ filePath: \"\" }` so read paths fail closed with `caller_error` rather than opening a temp database.\n- **F-EPIC-002**: Read-back surfaces (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listQueuedWork`) skip thread-reference validation present on the write path, so malformed references (e.g. empty path) reach storage open. Fix: route all read surfaces through the same `resolveThreadRef` validation used by writes; empty/invalid refs return `caller_error`/`thread_not_found` consistently at SDK and CLI layers. Add a small test per read surface for the empty-path and unknown-id legs.\n- **NB-2**: CLI parses flags with `strict: false`, silently ignoring unknown or misspelled flags (e.g. `--file-pth`). Fix: enable strict flag parsing in the CLI arg parser and return the existing structured usage error (`caller_error` with the CLI-adapter code pattern) naming the unknown flag; keep exit code 1. Update/extend the CLI process suite leg for an unknown-flag case.\n- **NB-5**: Dead code and stale artifacts. Remove the uncalled `notImplemented()` helper from `shared/errors.ts` (all stubs are gone since Story 5). Clean stale pre-epic compiled output from `dist/` (`dist/commands/`, `dist/thread-events/`, `dist/token-counting/`) — add a `prebuild` clean (e.g. `rm -rf dist` before `tsc`) or equivalent so `dist/` always reflects current `src/`.\n\nOut of scope for this batch (tracked separately): NB-1 (empty-string payload text — pending human ruling on epic-vs-tech-design conflict), NB-4 (test seams are sanctioned by the test plan's architecture-risk rows; no change), work_item constraint vocabulary (Epic 02 owns lifecycle schema).\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
