{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017odMyNQMJYJoceAXZBhTCn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four fix items are applied and both gates are green. Here is the result.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"applied\",\n  \"fixBatchPath\": \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/fix/001-epic-fix-batch.md\",\n  \"filesChanged\": [\n    \"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/index.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/cli/render.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/package.json\",\n    \"packages/lhc/vitest.config.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/test/epic-fix.test.ts\",\n    \"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-fix.test.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"changeSummary\": {\n    \"F-EPIC-001\": \"Added a blank-path guard (`isBlankPath`, trim-empty check) in the threads domain. `newThread` rejects empty/whitespace-only `filePath` with a `caller_error` (new code `invalid_thread_ref`) before any storage touch, so no temp database opens and no registry row is written. Mirrored the same guard in `resolveThreadRef`'s `{ filePath }` branch so read paths fail closed. New code `invalid_thread_ref` added to the SDK `ErrorCode` union (the batch specified `caller_error` but no code).\",\n    \"F-EPIC-002\": \"Read surfaces now validate the thread reference. `listMessages`, `listTurns`, and both `listQueuedWork` already route through `resolveThreadRef`, which now rejects blank paths; `listEvents` keeps its existing closed-envelope `validateThreadRef`. All read surfaces return `caller_error` on an empty path and `thread_not_found` on an unknown id, consistently. At the CLI, the four read commands (`messages list`, `messages list-queued-work`, `turns list`, `turns list-queued-work`) now emit the same `missing_flag` usage error as the intake commands when neither `--thread-id` nor `--file-path` is given (via shared `requireThreadRef`), instead of defaulting the path to '' and reaching storage.\",\n    \"NB-2\": \"CLI flag parsing switched from `strict: false` to `strict: true`. `parseFlags` catches the parse error and returns it as data; `runCli` renders an unknown/misspelled flag as a structured `caller_error` with new CLI-adapter code `unknown_flag`, naming the offending flag, exit code 1. No flags are silently dropped.\",\n    \"NB-5\": \"Removed the uncalled `notImplemented()` helper from `shared/errors.ts` (verified zero callers). Added a `clean` script (`rm -rf dist`) invoked by `build` (`pnpm run clean && tsc`) — chosen over a bare `prebuild` hook because pnpm's pre/post-script default is version-dependent; this guarantees the clean runs on every build. Verified post-build that the stale pre-epic dirs `dist/commands`, `dist/thread-events`, `dist/token-counting` are gone and `dist/` now mirrors `src/`.\"\n  },\n  \"testsAdded\": {\n    \"test/epic-fix.test.ts\": \"New Green-phase suite (runs under green-verify): SDK blank-path rejection for newThread (empty + whitespace) and resolveThreadRef with no registry row/file; per-read-surface empty-path (caller_error) and unknown-id (thread_not_found) legs; in-process CLI legs for empty --file-path, unknown flag named back, and missing-flag on all four read commands.\",\n    \"test/cli-process-fix.test.ts\": \"New process-boundary suite (gated to verify-all via vitest.config.ts exclude list, like the other cli-process suites): unknown-flag and empty --file-path observed through the spawned dist/cli.js.\"\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"story gate (green-verify)\",\n      \"command\": \"pnpm --dir packages/lhc run green-verify\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"detail\": \"build+typecheck+lint+boundaries clean; 12 test files / 118 tests passed; test-immutability OK (15 Red-phase files unchanged).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"epic gate (verify-all)\",\n      \"command\": \"pnpm --dir packages/lhc run verify-all\",\n      \"result\": \"pass\",\n      \"detail\": \"red-verify clean; 18 test files / 132 tests passed (includes process suites + new cli-process-fix legs).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedConcerns\": [\n    \"Deliberate, non-blocking: an empty-path reference yields `invalid_event` on the intake-stream read surface (`listEvents`, via the closed event-envelope schema shared with the write path) but `invalid_thread_ref` on the messages/turns read surfaces (via resolveThreadRef). Both are `caller_error`, satisfying F-EPIC-002's stated consistency (errorClass caller_error on empty path; thread_not_found on unknown id). Unifying the code further would require threads importing intake-stream's validator, which the boundary check forbids, or altering write-path validation, which Red-immutable tests pin to `invalid_event`.\",\n    \"Two new error codes were introduced where the batch said `caller_error` without prescribing one: SDK `invalid_thread_ref` and CLI-adapter `unknown_flag`.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Re-run the canonical epic review against this branch to confirm the F-EPIC-001 blocker is cleared and F-EPIC-002/NB-2/NB-5 are resolved; the out-of-scope items (NB-1 human ruling, NB-4 sanctioned seams, work_item vocabulary owned by Epic 02) remain tracked separately and were not touched.\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4203,"cache_read_input_tokens":118203,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4203},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"36778e1e-3bb5-45c6-8164-3cc17eb2f31a","uuid":"444ecc9d-92ee-47fc-8100-78ed15de1f90","request_id":"req_011CbuqjiQ63Au6b4aAqkQ2U"}
